Z||000000||Mach10||07-03-2001||08:23 PM||||Firstly, I'd like to thank Cliff for his email. Thank you for your trust. Be assured that I will advertize that link to whoever I can. Too bad I lost my list of contacts  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> during my last reformat...<P>I know I'm not the first to offer suggestions, but I think we should centralize the conversation.<BR>So lets start getting this back together.<P>Firstly, I'd like to make a few points:<BR>1) Cliff, you are working too hard, too much workload for this "free" service<BR>2) This forum is large.<BR>3) This forum is important to the Fiero Community<BR>4) This forum is getting out of hand.<P>All of these things come together to make an emotional and unstable environment. As much as I hate to admit it, this forum needs to be monitored fairly frequently to nip flame-wars in the bud before they come to flower, so to speak. What I would propose is as follows:<BR>-Additional moderators. First and foremost, these would be invaluable. Of course, carefull selection is important, as well as strict guidelines. Giving additional people the ability to at least temporarily ban users (subject to review by Cliff of course) for unnacceptable behavior would be a tremendous asset.<BR>-I think the time has come to make some concrete rules for all topics, O/T especially. Forbid things such as sexual harrassment, rascial slurs etc.<BR>-While the idea of using scripts to moderate things does have certain merit, I would suggest prudence here. Computers are stupid, and this can be abused easily. As for the auto-ignore, basing it on personal preference is a nice feature, but automating it to globally ignore might be troublesome. Especially since many members quote the offensive party anyway. <P>------------------<BR>"Duct Tape is Good to Mach 3"||||reg||1
