Z||000014||Fformula88||07-04-2001||05:31 PM||||Unfortunately self restraint won't stop everything.  Thats not realistic.  However, going too far could destroy what is good with this forum.<P>Even without moderators, it is overall a low flame board compared to many others.  Cliff, or anybody else shouldn't have to babysit a forum everyday to try and shut down posts for offensive material.  On the other hand, it may be a good idea to allow some of the long time members (and I'm thinking of a couple specific original, or very long time people) who are very well repected by the community to have some say over closing posts down, or at least being able to send Cliff special requests to lock a post down.<P>The voting idea also seems to be a good solution from another post.  Any member would eb able to click on a botton in a thread which would notify cliff that it has been voted for closing.  If a thread received a lot of this vote he could review it and close it down if necessary.  If cliff truted anyone else with this responsibility, they could respond to these threads too.<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000015||Mach10||07-04-2001||05:43 PM||||I would have to agree. Long term, trusted members could be chosen as moderators. In fact, we could first have a "nomination" vote, and then a vote on which "N" of the nominees would get in. How's that, Cliff?||||reg||6
Z||000016||JohnnyK||07-04-2001||06:31 PM||||Or, we could leave it as is. This is the friendliest board on the net. No real flames, nothing.. I still have yet to see something really offensive.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Mach10||07-05-2001||02:19 AM||||No, I definitly think that something should be done. Cliff appears to have had about enough of it. Believe it or not, there still seems to be a problem. Read Cliff's post here:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/008562-2.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/008562-2.html</A> <BR>And tell me again why everything should stay the same. Of course, nothing can be done without Cliff's permission anyways. This topic was started with the intent of finding ways to make things a little easier on Cliff. There HAVE been increasing complaints about the O/T section, for example. I would agree that yes, we are pretty friendly here, but I will not go as far as to say that nothing is wrong.<P>**EDIT** Oh yes, this post was created while PFF was still "down." I had emailed Cliff about the take down, and he informed me that he needed a place to discuss changes. That's what I set about doing. Obviously it's back up, but it's too late to change the name, and yes, the urgency is somewhat diminished. <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 07-05-2001).]||||reg||13
Z||000018||84Bill||07-05-2001||10:47 AM||||I think the vote thing might be a good idea.<BR>there are pros and cons to it that I can see right off the bat. I don't think there really is a need for it since this Forum is a very decent one, almost self cleaning  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Pros<BR>1 Minimizes emails to Cliff regarding silly complaints<BR>2 Makes members more proactive<BR>3 Will bring to light problem ares and individuals<P>Cons<BR>1 Makes members more opinionated about content<BR>2 It will close hot debates if a thread is voted off.<BR>3 It will close "unwanted" threads just because it is perceived as unimportant or "stupid"<P>I think power to the people is a good thing but people are different and that's what makes the world turn. If we start a vote process it could lead to factional and clique groups and spawn problems of a different kind. <P>Moderators would be a better solution<BR>If Cliff is looking for moderators for this board there should be one for each topic area and they should be very objective individuals with tolerances for a wide range of things. <P>They are only there to report problems to Cliff and ONLY give "advice" to individuals in a respectful way, that's about all they should be able to do. No kick power, No power to close threads, anything like that should be left to Cliff. They should be respectful at all times. If a moderator is not respectful he or she is not effectively doing the job correctly. and a moderators head is always on the chopping block.<P>I personally don't read topics from certain individuals because I don't particularly like what they have to say most of the time but as a moderator I would have to read and understand what the majority of the posts have in order to make a judgement. That judgement is basically my opinion compared to all others opinions I would have read. <P>Take 85blackgt's thread about punching out the Toys-R-Us geraffe, I have read it and I would ask it be closed judging by the negative responses. nearly 100% are negative and this is not the first thread from this individual that has been received in the way. To me it's not a problem , if he wants to look like an idiot and get spanked by nearly 100% of responses that's fine with me. BUT should this thread start getting out of hand then it should be removed, as it stands right now IMO it's fine.<BR>I have said it before, Cliff has done an exemplary job at handling this Forum. <BR>I know he reads almost if not every thread on it, I'm sure not every post every day but enough to know what's happening in a more than general way. <P>IMO<BR>This forum is in decent shape. There are many members with many opinions and for the most part it's been civilized. If Cliff needs help he will ask and I'm sure there will be 1000 volunteers myself included.<BR>Peace  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Sheesh<BR>I think I broke the spell checker with this one   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000019||saleenfiero||07-05-2001||02:49 PM||||Hell I'd pay to use this.  It would keep the numbers of the forum down, which would eliminate ALOT of people who have just signed up and never come back, but have information  just taking up space.||||reg||1
